From: phpv <https://github.com/supanadit/phpv>
Subject: [PATCH] drop -traditional-cpp for old PHP on macOS

PHP 4.0-4.2's configure appends -traditional-cpp to CPPFLAGS on Darwin.
Clang in Xcode 16 no longer accepts that flag, so Zend fails to compile.
The generated parser sources do not need it; skip the flag.
---
 a/configure | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -2059,7 +2059,7 @@
     ;;
 *dgux*)
     CPPFLAGS="$CPPFLAGS -D_BSD_TIMEOFDAY_FLAVOR";;
 *darwin*|*rhapsody*)
-    CPPFLAGS="$CPPFLAGS -traditional-cpp";;
+    ;;
 *bsdi*)
     BSD_MAKEFILE=yes;;
-- 
2.47.1

